    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An archipelago of some 17,000 islands, proclaimed independent in 1945 and recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> after a four-year revolution.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sukarno">Sukarno</a>'s Guided Democracy gave way after the killings of 1965–1966 to Suharto's military-backed New Order.</li><li>Since 1998 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indonesia">Indonesia</a> has been a decentralised democracy, a G20 economy and the most populous Muslim-majority country.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Indonesian, the national language, was chosen in 1928 from Malay, a trading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lingua-franca">lingua franca</a>, rather than Javanese, the mother tongue of the largest ethnic group.</p></aside>
    </section>

